{"problem": "dedupe\n\nReturn only dedupe elements of a sequence\n\n>>> tuple(dedupe((1, 2, 3)))\n(1, 2, 3)\n>>> tuple(dedupe((1, 2, 1, 3)))\n(1, 2, 3)\n\nUniqueness can be defined by key keyword\n\n>>> tuple(dedupe(['cat', 'mouse', 'dog', 'hen'], key=len))\n('cat', 'mouse')", "resolution": "def dedupe(seq, key=None):\n    \"\"\" Return only dedupe elements of a sequence\n\n    >>> tuple(dedupe((1, 2, 3)))\n    (1, 2, 3)\n    >>> tuple(dedupe((1, 2, 1, 3)))\n    (1, 2, 3)\n\n    Uniqueness can be defined by key keyword\n\n    >>> tuple(dedupe(['cat', 'mouse', 'dog', 'hen'], key=len))\n    ('cat', 'mouse')\n    \"\"\"\n    seen = set()\n    seen_add = seen.add\n    if key is None:\n        for item in seq:\n            if item not in seen:\n                seen_add(item)\n                yield item\n    else:  # calculate key\n        for item in seq:\n            val = key(item)\n            if val not in seen:\n                seen_add(val)\n                yield item\n", "text": "dedupe"}